.TH TEXTIFYOPENDOCUMENT "1" "2026-10-24" "textifyopendocument 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
textifyopendocument \- fast OpenDocument to plain text converter for previews
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B textifyopendocument
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILENAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
textifyopendocument extracts plain text from OpenDocument files (text,
spreadsheets, presentations) using streaming XML parsing. It is designed for
file-manager previews: a single pass replaces the regular-expression pipeline
of the original odt2txt, which became extremely slow on large documents.
.PP
The FILENAME argument is mandatory. Output goes to standard output unless
\fB\-\-output\fR is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR=\fIWIDTH\fR
Wrap text lines after \fIWIDTH\fR characters. The default is 65. A word
longer than the width is never split. If \fIWIDTH\fR is \-1, no lines are
broken. Values below 3 (other than \-1) are invalid.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Write output to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Print the raw content.xml of the document, unprocessed.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-input\fR
Treat the input file as a raw XML file (fodt, fods, ...) instead of a zip.
.TP
\fB\-\-encoding\fR=\fIX\fR
Convert the output to encoding \fIX\fR unconditionally. Without this option,
the terminal encoding is detected from LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, then LANG,
defaulting to UTF\-8. With \fB\-\-encoding\fR=\fIshow\fR, print the encoding
that would be used and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-subst\fR=\fISUBST\fR
Select which non\-ascii characters are replaced by ascii look\-a\-likes.
Valid values are \fIall\fR (replace every character for which a
substitution is known), \fIsome\fR (replace characters the output encoding
cannot represent; the default), and \fInone\fR (replace nothing; characters
the output encoding cannot represent become question marks).
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\-chars\fR=\fIN\fR
Truncated preview mode: stop after \fIN\fR characters of output (Unicode
scalar values, newlines included) and skip converting the rest of the file.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\-time\fR=\fIN\fR
Truncated preview mode: stop converting after \fIN\fR milliseconds. If both
limits are given, whichever fires first wins.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Accepted for compatibility with odt2txt; ignored.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help.
.SH ATTRIBUTION
textifyopendocument reimagines odt2txt by Dennis Stosberg
(https://github.com/dstosberg/odt2txt), whose tool and whose advice to
replace the regular-expression approach with XML parsing inspired this
project.
